en","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MDk3MzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/commits/c4a63fe5a8d14f4336a157b8a8f12da0e2d96814/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T17:37:41Z","email":"kigen.work@gmail.com","name":"Dennis Kigen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T17:38:57Z","email":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ian"},"message":"fix: leave a clean scaffold and reject contradictory flags (#24)","tree":{"sha":"7e25fb24d7cf1dd81e433d131fe9aa177a5f3a87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/git/trees/7e25fb24d7cf1dd81e433d131fe9aa177a5f3a87"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/git/commits/c4a63fe5a8d14f4336a157b8a8f12da0e2d96814","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52504170?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ibacher","id":52504170,"login":"ibacher","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNTA0MTcw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/create-o3-app/commit/c4a63fe5a8d14f4336a157b8a8f12da0e2d96814","node_id":"C_kwDOQz_jx9oAKGM0YTYzZmU1YThkMTRmNDMzNmExNTdiOGE4ZjEyZGEwZTJkOTY4MTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/create-o3-app/commit/7165392486f8165c58c979cc6633c57d0414c33a","sha":"7165392486f8165c58c979cc6633c57d0414c33a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/commits/7165392486f8165c58c979cc6633c57d0414c33a"}],"sha":"c4a63fe5a8d14f4336a157b8a8f12da0e2d96814","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/commits/c4a63fe5a8d14f4336a157b8a8f12da0e2d96814"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8509731?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/denniskigen","id":8509731,"login":"denniskigen","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MDk3MzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/commits/7165392486f8165c58c979cc6633c57d0414c33a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T10:29:55Z","email":"kigen.work@gmail.com","name":"denniskigen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T17:38:57Z","email":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ian"},"message":"fix: keep monorepo generation coherent\n\nFour monorepo defects, each verified by reproducing it first.\n\nThe pnpm workspace updater edited YAML line by line, so a valid inline\ndeclaration like `packages: [\"packages/*\"]` was not recognized as a\n`packages:` line: the updater appended a second `packages` key and the\nfile no longer parsed, since YAML map keys must be unique. It now parses\nand serializes with the `yaml` package, which also preserves the user''s\ncomments, handles inline and block lists, and refuses to rewrite a file\nthat was already invalid rather than compounding the damage. `yaml` was\nalready installed transitively and is now a direct dependency.\n\n`--monorepo` reported success against an ordinary project: the package\nwas generated, no root configuration changed, and nothing joined it to a\nworkspace. The generator now refuses before writing unless the root\ndeclares `workspaces` in package.json or has a pnpm-workspace.yaml, and\npoints at --new-monorepo or --standalone instead.\n\nThe generated package carried `packageManager` and `.yarnrc.yml`, so a\nchild install and a root install could disagree about the Yarn version\nand the linker. Both now belong to the monorepo root, which\n`--new-monorepo` writes, and are omitted from packages generated inside\na monorepo.\n\n`--new-monorepo` guarded only the future package directory, so an\nunrelated non-empty root was still given a manifest, a README, a\n.gitignore, and a package directory. The guard now covers the root.\n\nVerified end to end: an inline pnpm declaration is extended into valid\nYAML with its comment intact; `--monorepo` in an ordinary project and\n`--new-monorepo` into a non-empty root both refuse without writing; and\nin a generated monorepo, `yarn install` at the root leaves the child\npackage typechecking, testing, and building.","tree":{"sha":"708f00cde1125d1713ab1e70df6dbe9ba33b380c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/git/trees/708f00cde1125d1713ab1e70df6dbe9ba33b380c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/git/commits/7165392486f8165c58c979cc6633c57d0414c33a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52504170?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ibacher","id":52504170,"login":"ibacher","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNTA0MTcw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/create-o3-app/commit/7165392486f8165c58c979cc6633c57d0414c33a","node_id":"C_kwDOQz_jx9oAKDcxNjUzOTI0ODZmODE2NWM1OGM5NzljYzY2MzNjNTdkMDQxNGMzM2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/create-o3-app/commit/d86ef31cf4151666281a5be6bdd2f91f019b0cd6","sha":"d86ef31cf4151666281a5be6bdd2f91f019b0cd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/commits/d86ef31cf4151666281a5be6bdd2f91f019b0cd6"}],"sha":"7165392486f8165c58c979cc6633c57d0414c33a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/commits/7165392486f8165c58c979cc6633c57d0414c33a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8509731?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/denniskigen","id":8509731,"login":"denniskigen","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MDk3MzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/commits/d86ef31cf4151666281a5be6bdd2f91f019b0cd6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T10:24:10Z","email":"kigen.work@gmail.com","name":"denniskigen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T17:38:57Z","email":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ian"},"message":"fix: generate component names that always compile\n\nValid project names could derive component names that break the\ngenerated module. A project named `react` derived a component named\n`React`, so the page rendered `const React: React.FC` beside\n`import React from ''react''` and the module failed to compile with\nTS2300, TS2604, and TS2786. A project named `123-app` derived `123App`,\nwhich is not a valid identifier and failed the module config schema with\nan unhelpful \"Invalid module configuration\" at the end of the run.\n\nComponent names are now checked against the identifiers the generated\nfiles actually bring into scope: the imports in the component templates\n(React, Layer, Tile, Button, the modal and workspace imports,\nBrowserRouter, Routes, Route, Root) and the declarations in index.ts,\nwhose camelCase lifecycle export a name like `Options` or `ConfigSchema`\nwould redeclare. The check runs in the component-name prompts and again\nin the engine, so a name supplied by --route-component is rejected too,\nwith a message that names the conflict.\n\nThe default component derived from the project name is now sanitized\nrather than rejected: leading digits are dropped and the result\nrecapitalized (`123-app` gives `App`, `2fa-setup` gives `FaSetup`), and\na derived name that would collide is suffixed (`react` gives\n`ReactPage`). A test asserts every derived name satisfies the component\nname schema and the reserved check, so the CLI cannot generate a name it\nwould refuse.\n\nVerified end to end: `create-o3-app react` now generates ReactPage in\nreact-page.component.tsx and the module installs, typechecks, lints, and\nbuilds; `create-o3-app 123-app` generates App instead of failing; and\n--route-component React is rejected with the explanatory message.","tree":{"sha":"5b506287948dca8108e6c4c287ed0c349e9e601e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/git/trees/5b506287948dca8108e6c4c287ed0c349e9e601e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/git/commits/d86ef31cf4151666281a5be6bdd2f91f019b0cd6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52504170?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibacher/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ibacher","id":52504170,"login":"ibacher","node_id":"