tps://api.github.com/users/denniskigen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/commits/e49f2ae6ef0223063800dda47593b4b3729a27aa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T09:05:57Z","email":"kigen.work@gmail.com","name":"denniskigen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T09:05:57Z","email":"kigen.work@gmail.com","name":"denniskigen"},"message":"chore: release v1.2.0","tree":{"sha":"a779af24abea1cfcd25249832cd737ccb998c60d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/git/trees/a779af24abea1cfcd25249832cd737ccb998c60d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/git/commits/e49f2ae6ef0223063800dda47593b4b3729a27aa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8509731?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/denniskigen","id":8509731,"login":"denniskigen","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MDk3MzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/create-o3-app/commit/e49f2ae6ef0223063800dda47593b4b3729a27aa","node_id":"C_kwDOQz_jx9oAKGU0OWYyYWU2ZWYwMjIzMDYzODAwZGRhNDc1OTNiNGIzNzI5YTI3YWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/create-o3-app/commit/adc83f2402697197494b42f51367c0460202e60d","sha":"adc83f2402697197494b42f51367c0460202e60d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/commits/adc83f2402697197494b42f51367c0460202e60d"}],"sha":"e49f2ae6ef0223063800dda47593b4b3729a27aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/commits/e49f2ae6ef0223063800dda47593b4b3729a27aa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8509731?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/denniskigen","id":8509731,"login":"denniskigen","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MDk3MzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/commits/adc83f2402697197494b42f51367c0460202e60d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T08:59:18Z","email":"kigen.work@gmail.com","name":"Dennis Kigen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T08:59:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: generate workspaces using the Workspace2 API (#21)\n\n* feat: generate Workspace2 workspaces\n\nThe workspace template used the v1 contract (`DefaultWorkspaceProps`\nand a bare component registered under `workspaces` with a `type`).\nCurrent O3 code overwhelmingly uses the Workspace2 API: 92 files across\npatient-chart and patient-management versus 3 on the old contract. The\nv1 contract still works, so this is modernization, but a scaffold\nshould not start new modules on the legacy default.\n\nThe generated workspace component is now typed with\n`Workspace2DefinitionProps`, renders inside `<Workspace2 title={...}>`\n(the title moves from routes.json into the component, where it is also\ntranslatable), and closes via the injected `closeWorkspace`. The\nroutes.json template registers the Workspace2 triple: a\n`workspaceGroups2` entry scoped to the module''s first route, one\n`workspaceWindows2` entry, and the `workspaces2` entries attached to\nit, matching the shape esm-appointments-app uses.\n\nThe workspace `type` prompt and field are removed: Workspace2 has no\ntype, since the window and group model replaces the type-based\nexclusivity.\n\nVerified end to end: a scaffold with a workspace installs, typechecks,\nlints, and builds against @openmrs/esm-framework@next, and its\nroutes.json carries the three registration sections.\n\n* Document the generated workspace group scope in the README\n\nThe Workspace2 group is scoped to the module''s first route by design;\nmodules with more routes, or extension-only modules, need to widen the\nscopePattern themselves. The generated README now says so next to the\nother workspace guidance.\n\n* Anchor the generated workspace scope pattern\n\nThe Workspace2 navigation logic treats scopePattern as a regex and\ndev-warns when it lacks a start anchor. The generated pattern is now\n`^<first-route>`, and the no-route fallback becomes `^/`: the previous\n`/<project-name>` fallback could never match an extension-only\nmodule''s host page, so its workspace closed on the next same-app\nnavigation. The README wording and route test expectations follow, and\nthe now-unused toKebabCase import is dropped from the engine.","tree":{"sha":"fb3c88a49a7edd29066c2b766a5d160188cca611","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/git/trees/fb3c88a49a7edd29066c2b766a5d160188cca611"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/git/commits/adc83f2402697197494b42f51367c0460202e60d","verification":{"payload":"tree fb3c88a49a7edd29066c2b766a5d160188cca611\nparent 945e7a70815c0e6294c9e8ff9a30d6a89dd6e94c\nauthor Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com> 1786093158 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786093158 +0300\n\nfeat: generate workspaces using the Workspace2 API (#21)\n\n* feat: generate Workspace2 workspaces\n\nThe workspace template used the v1 contract (`DefaultWorkspaceProps`\nand a bare component registered under `workspaces` with a `type`).\nCurrent O3 code overwhelmingly uses the Workspace2 API: 92 files across\npatient-chart and patient-management versus 3 on the old contract. The\nv1 contract still works, so this is modernization, but a scaffold\nshould not start new modules on the legacy default.\n\nThe generated workspace component is now typed with\n`Workspace2DefinitionProps`, renders inside `<Workspace2 title={...}>`\n(the title moves from routes.json into the component, where it is also\ntranslatable), and closes via the injected `closeWorkspace`. The\nroutes.json template registers the Workspace2 triple: a\n`workspaceGroups2` entry scoped to the module''s first route, one\n`workspaceWindows2` entry, and the `workspaces2` entries attached to\nit, matching the shape esm-appointments-app uses.\n\nThe workspace `type` prompt and field are removed: Workspace2 has no\ntype, since the window and group model replaces the type-based\nexclusivity.\n\nVerified end to end: a scaffold with a workspace installs, typechecks,\nlints, and builds against @openmrs/esm-framework@next, and its\nroutes.json carries the three registration sections.\n\n* Document the generated workspace group scope in the README\n\nThe Workspace2 group is scoped to the module''s first route by design;\nmodules with more routes, or extension-only modules, need to widen the\nscopePattern themselves. The generated README now says so next to the\nother workspace guidance.\n\n* Anchor the generated workspace scope pattern\n\nThe Workspace2 navigation logic treats scopePattern as a regex and\ndev-warns when it lacks a start anchor. The generated pattern is now\n`^<first-route>`, and the no-route fallback becomes `^/`: the previous\n`/<project-name>` fallback could never match an extension-only\nmodule''s host page, so its workspace closed on the next same-app\nnavigation. The README wording and route test expectations follow, and\nthe now-unused toKebabCase import is dropped from the engine.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqdZ5mCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4q0QAKS2YllMzBhOUi8g8bhPvReU\nz1Qr0s65hrWqBFtmdUwlnViVD12huBnIbBqMu92p40tbNdRXnMP4oG+Y1AQzWhn/\nTUZsVgQLDwOAzJYirY8TNsmA5bcfFfMj+j+M6VoFxKqxhOWZBP1ucWpRKaVIl2mF\nCFzo80w9w2J3mwGxApYtk/ydd4HxV6vv9W8hS1jOioSHkSl7V7C6uCF/JxjbuYcF\nAcMxCdEpVQkDzl2+PTrUACa+VqiKFd+gYG2dnwbdRHRFHqE6+0DKmeyMpYKGcRYJ\n5QPdMQ2gcQJDfHGbc7zf5J5BeS2HfnimAOsC8oD4LYYdiD/ejB/Wr4kBgo9+dmYF\nK8hWZNKZcyUvTCuemHFBV2VCa2zQNyn0SX7o4cibWPsOw8dWIXwHIfGDcPPn44Mz\nBa2OLCg8mpC6wQN5CWvBcCPSf1+JqrYTmnvvgxoJo08qJlF/65apHao01nficSoR\ngEiz4sel09cFuCu7e/JX/IThrlH3WiHHP7nN9jy5gWLS1+YedzEEn9L3U/i/oVpD\n231P1gGO+f6IMw8l93NnpIsVJ0743Mp3dVPWtXaw8IXWsA+9+yzwgBcM2pd7wg0E\nqIhpGneeqx9PwgI+KdAUooybJMLQZlMvcp1Ti4zJOUwmVMcNhhMg1l4JacbDT0Br\nMQbB64cmww/qTIBmWX2p\n=HBr5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-07T08:59:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"