","html_url":"https://github.com/denniskigen","id":8509731,"login":"denniskigen","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MDk3MzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/create-o3-app/commit/4d92a28d092670aa0ce8520ec73ffd0abae411a7","node_id":"C_kwDOQz_jx9oAKDRkOTJhMjhkMDkyNjcwYWEwY2U4NTIwZWM3M2ZmZDBhYmFlNDExYTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/create-o3-app/commit/46395fc3659f80305f70e08812bab8efcc382d02","sha":"46395fc3659f80305f70e08812bab8efcc382d02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/commits/46395fc3659f80305f70e08812bab8efcc382d02"}],"sha":"4d92a28d092670aa0ce8520ec73ffd0abae411a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/commits/4d92a28d092670aa0ce8520ec73ffd0abae411a7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8509731?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/denniskigen","id":8509731,"login":"denniskigen","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MDk3MzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/commits/46395fc3659f80305f70e08812bab8efcc382d02/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T21:24:56Z","email":"kigen.work@gmail.com","name":"Dennis Kigen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T21:24:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: generate modals, workspaces, and feature flags from the prompts (#13)\n\n* feat: generate modals, workspaces, and feature flags from the prompts\n\nThe modals, workspaces, and feature flags prompts collected a yes/no\nanswer and then stopped at a TODO, leaving `config.modals` and friends\nas empty arrays that Handlebars treats as falsy. The `routes.json` and\n`index.ts` templates were already wired to render these sections, so\nanswering yes produced nothing. The prompts now collect the actual\nentries in loops modeled on the extensions flow, and the engine\ngenerates a component and stylesheet per modal and per workspace from\nnew templates (a Carbon `ModalHeader`/`ModalBody`/`ModalFooter` shell\ntaking a `closeModal` prop, and a `DefaultWorkspaceProps` workspace\nwith a `ButtonSet` footer).\n\nFixes two template bugs found along the way:\n\n- `routes.json` emitted `\"name\"` for feature flags where the routes\n  schema requires `\"flagName\"`.\n- `index.ts` passed an import thunk to `getSyncLifecycle`, which takes\n  a component, so the generated extension exports were broken.\n  Extension exports now use `getAsyncLifecycle`, matching template-app.\n\nVerified by scaffolding a module with a route, an extension, a modal,\na workspace, and a feature flag: `yarn typescript`, `yarn lint`,\n`yarn test`, and `yarn build` all pass in the generated output.\n\n* Fix modal scaffolding review findings\n\nStandalone projects now enter the documented interactive prompt flow when no non-interactive flags are provided. Generated modals use the framework-injected close prop, and routes metadata preserves free-text values through JSON serialization.\n\nAdd focused coverage for interactive collection, modal close wiring, and special-character handling.\n\n* Accept any workspace type string\n\nThe workspace type prompt restricted the answer to form, chart, or\nother, but the framework contract types `type` as a plain string and\nreal workspaces use custom types like `patient-search-workspace`.\nSince workspaces of the same type replace each other and share the\nright-sidebar icon, forcing unrelated custom workspaces onto `other`\nwould wrongly make them mutually exclusive.\n\nThe prompt is now free text with `form` (the framework default) as the\ninitial value, the answer is trimmed, and the `WorkspaceConfig` type\nand schema accept any non-empty string. Includes schema tests for\ncustom and whitespace-only types and an interactive prompt test.\n\n* Generate modals and workspaces with their O3 file suffixes\n\nO3 encodes the component kind in the file suffix: patient-chart has 21\n`.modal.tsx` files and none named `*modal*.component.tsx`, and the\ntemplate''s own extract-translations glob already expected\n`src/**/*.modal.tsx`. Generated modals and workspaces now use\n`.modal.tsx` and `.workspace.tsx` instead of `.component.tsx`, the\n`index.ts` imports follow, and `src/**/*.workspace.tsx` is added to the\nextract-translations globs so workspace strings reach the catalog.\n\nVerified end to end on a scaffold with all five construct types:\n`yarn typescript`, `yarn lint`, `yarn test`, and `yarn build` pass, and\n`yarn extract-translations` parses all six source files and emits the\nmodal and workspace keys into `translations/en.json`.\n\n* Strip the component kind from generated modal and workspace basenames\n\n`DeleteThingModal` previously emitted `delete-thing-modal.modal.tsx`,\nrepeating the kind that the O3 file suffix already encodes. The file\nand stylesheet basenames now strip a trailing `Modal` or `Workspace`\nbefore kebab-casing (`delete-thing.modal.tsx`, `delete-thing.scss`),\nmatching the ecosystem pattern where `create-queue-entry.workspace.tsx`\nexports `CreateQueueEntryWorkspace`. The React component names,\nlifecycle export names, and routes.json component references keep the\nfull component name. Component names without the suffix pass through\nunchanged, and a name that is exactly `Modal` or `Workspace` is not\nstripped to an empty basename.\n\n* Escape free-text workspace types in routes.json\n\nThe workspace `type` accepts any non-empty string since the free-text\nchange, but the template still interpolated it raw: Handlebars HTML-\nescapes quotes into `&quot;` and passes backslashes through, so a type\nlike `custom \"quoted\" \\ type` corrupts or breaks the generated\n`routes.json`. It now renders through the `json` helper like title,\nlabel, and description already do. The latent `meta` interpolation had\nthe same defect with double-stash HTML escaping and is fixed the same\nway, though nothing populates it yet.\n\n* Fail fast on generated file collisions\n\n`DeleteThingModal` and `DeleteThing` are distinct valid component\nnames, but both derive `delete-thing.modal.tsx` and `delete-thing.scss`,\nso the later entry silently overwrote the first while `index.ts` still\nexported both lifecycles. Modal and workspace stylesheets could collide\nthe same way across kinds.\n\n`generateFiles` now claims every derived component and stylesheet path\nup front across pages, extensions, modals, and workspaces, and throws a\n`ValidationError` naming both components when two different components\nclaim the same file. The same component reused across entries of one\nkind renders identical content, so it is not treated as a collision.\n\n* Reject repeated component claims in the collision check\n\nThe check previously allowed one component to back multiple entries of\na kind on the reasoning that the generated file content was identical.\nThat validated the wrong surface: repeated routes emit duplicate\nimports in root.component.tsx, repeated extensions, modals, and\nworkspaces emit duplicate lifecycle exports in index.ts, and modal and\nworkspace files interpolate entry-specific fallback text, so the later\nrender overwrites the first with different content. Any repeated claim\nnow fails with a message that distinguishes a component configured more\nthan once from two components colliding on a derived basename.\n\n* Guard the static root component files from generated collisions\n\nThe collision check only covered generated-versus-generated paths. A\npage or extension component named `Root`, or a modal or workspace whose\nstripped basename is `root`, derives root.component.tsx or root.scss\nand would silently overwrite the static root component that index.ts\nmounts as the app root. The static basenames are now claimed before any\nderived ones, so those names fail with the same clear collision error.","tree":{"sha":"5ae241d02407dcf778afcda0182d86ab8381e7a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/git/trees/5ae241d02407dcf778afcda0182d86ab8381e7a7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/git/commits/46395fc3659f80305f70e08812bab8efcc382d02","verification":{"payload":"tree 5ae241d02407dcf778afcda0182d86ab8381e7a7\nparent f1403f25e38b1d6e7cc1c7edd8c88af9477554bf\nauthor Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com> 1785965096 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785965096 +0300\n\nfeat: generate modals, workspaces, and feature flags from the prompts (#13)\n\n* feat: generate modals, workspaces, and feature flags from the prompts\n\nThe modals, workspaces, and feature flags prompts collected a yes/no\nanswer and then stopped at a TODO, leaving `config.modals` and friends\nas empty arrays that Handlebars treats as falsy. The `routes.json` and\n`index.ts` templates were already wired to render these sections, so\nanswering yes produced nothing. The prompts now collect the actual\nentries in loops modeled on the extensions flow, and the engine\ngenerates a component and stylesheet per modal and per workspace from\nnew templates (a Carbon `ModalHeader`/`ModalBody`/`ModalFooter` shell\ntaking a `closeModal` prop, and a `DefaultWorkspaceProps` workspace\nwith a `ButtonSet` footer).\n\nFixes two template bugs found along the way:\n\n- `routes.json` emitted `\"name\"` for feature flags where the routes\n  schema requires `\"flagName\"`.\n- `index.ts` passed an import thunk to `getSyncLifecycle`, which takes\n  a component, so the generated extension exports were broken.\n  Extension exports now use `getAsyncLifecycle`, matching template-app.\n\nVerified by scaffolding a module with a route, an extension, a modal,\na workspace, and a feature flag: `yarn typescript`, `yarn lint`,\n`yarn test`, and `yarn build` all pass in the generated output.\n\n* Fix modal scaffolding review findings\n\nStandalone projects now enter the documented interactive prompt flow when no non-interactive flags are provided. Generated modals use the framework-injected close prop, and routes metadata preserves free-text values through JSON serialization.\n\nAdd focused coverage for interactive collection, modal close wiring, and special-character handling.\n\n* Accept any workspace type string\n\nThe workspace type prompt restricted the answer to form, chart, or\nother, but the framework contract types `type` as a plain string and\nreal workspaces use custom types like `patient-search-workspace`.\nSince workspaces of the same type replace each other and share the\nright-sidebar icon, forcing unrelated custom workspaces onto `other`\nwould wrongly make them mutually exclusive.\n\nThe prompt is now free text with `form` (the framework default) as the\ninitial value, the answer is trimmed, and the `WorkspaceConfig` type\nand schema accept any non-empty string. Includes schema tests for\ncustom and whitespace-only types and an interactive prompt test.\n\n* Generate modals and workspaces with their O3 file suffixes\n\nO3 encodes the component kind in the file suffix: patient-chart has 21\n`.modal.tsx` files and none named `*modal*.component.tsx`, and the\ntemplate''s own extract-translations glob already expected\n`src/**/*.modal.tsx`. Generated modals and workspaces now use\n`.modal.tsx` and `.workspace.tsx` instead of `.component.tsx`, the\n`index.ts` imports follow, and `src/**/*.workspace.tsx` is added to the\nextract-translations globs so workspace strings reach the catalog.\n\nVerified end to end on a scaffold with all five construct types:\n`yarn typescript`, `yarn lint`, `yarn test`, and `yarn build` pass, and\n`yarn extract-translations` parses all six source files and emits the\nmodal and workspace keys into `translations/en.json`.\n\n* Strip the component kind from generated modal and workspace basenames\n\n`DeleteThingModal` previously emitted `delete-thing-modal.modal.tsx`,\nrepeating the kind that the O3 file suffix already encodes. The file\nand stylesheet basenames now strip a trailing `Modal` or `Workspace`\nbefore kebab-casing (`delete-thing.modal.tsx`, `delete-thing.scss`),\nmatching the ecosystem pattern where `create-queue-entry.workspace.tsx`\nexports `CreateQueueEntryWorkspace`. The React component names,\nlifecycle export names, and routes.json component references keep the\nfull component name. Component names without the suffix pass through\nunchanged, and a name that is exactly `Modal` or `Workspace` is not\nstripped to an empty basename.\n\n* Escape free-text workspace types in routes.json\n\nThe workspace `type` accepts any non-empty string since the free-text\nchange, but the template still interpolated it raw: Handlebars HTML-\nescapes quotes into `&quot;` and passes backslashes through, so a type\nlike `custom \"quoted\" \\ type` corrupts or breaks the generated\n`routes.json`. It now renders through the `json` helper like title,\nlabel, and description already do. The latent `meta` interpolation had\nthe same defect with double-stash HTML escaping and is fixed the same\nway, though nothing populates it yet.\n\n* Fail fast on generated file collisions\n\n`DeleteThingModal` and `DeleteThing` are distinct valid component\nnames, but both derive `delete-thing.modal.tsx` and `delete-thing.scss`,\nso the later entry silently overwrote the first while `index.ts` still\nexported both lifecycles. Modal and workspace stylesheets could collide\nthe same way across kinds.\n\n`generateFiles` now claims every derived component and stylesheet path\nup front across pages, extensions, modals, and workspaces, and throws a\n`ValidationError` naming both components when two different components\nclaim the same file. The same component reused across entries of one\nkind renders identical content, so it is not treated as a collision.\n\n* Reject repeated component claims in the collision check\n\nThe check previously allowed one component to back multiple entries of\na kind on the reasoning that the generated file content was identical.\nThat validated the wrong surface: repeated routes emit duplicate\nimports in root.component.tsx, repeated extensions, modals, and\nworkspaces emit duplicate lifecycle exports in index.ts, and modal and\nworkspace files interpolate entry-specific fallback text, so the later\nrender overwrites the first with different content. Any repeated claim\nnow fails with a message that distinguishes a component configured more\nthan once from two components colliding on a derived basename.\n\n* Guard the static root component files from generated collisions\n\nThe collision check only covered generated-versus-generated paths. A\npage or extension component named `Root`, or a modal or workspace whose\nstripped basename is `root`, derives root.component.tsx or root.scss\nand would silently overwrite the static root component that index.ts\nmounts as the app root. The static basenames are now claimed before any\nderived ones, so those names fail with the same clear collision error.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqc6ooCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAncoQAC0+cfG5CrAXom+8NoASm/tq\nJmYe20S2N29NPtdbqvo9O772XVQOeZk5cuwURFnaZJku7H129n4Lf2O1/tN5ONmw\nYeyTjuZtAZHTL9pgZH6n4y5sC+mVAGrwW9ryP38HUrkNcX2B8zAhlJ9hNJT5vufR\nRm4ws0ZbIlo4SHhMuJFmqSIGR05irEtsvWAFdseX70vhmUxhHv7VudNKQIGixZOw\nn4OG8dd2BiOVXL84y0NomR3n/8vc31rCSAIyPCja2oRIOQXg8wGPXW8aIUnEBf+g\nUJN0SJruFMVkDxA0XoszgBDxnkldmUf/m7M09fFzkqzYjxYzsUbWp0A8OzVN79kT\nnE9SYt1NdvmpLFz9GEAmr4ZZ+NML6J2CqjsJnoZx/DAqDQNFBZGDuJXs9PjDrMtr\nxgoWlJOwwDuUeBzsO0wKmDQ/mFU7RM8mw/NSYiIFEFQYFewQaUfP66oPJ0wgUgGM\nwZ3ono6S5VQjBPnH0ZI/C/Ov0LbkKFz9RO+gBNUudKhlDcOwMqpiaAdhtavrl0CI\n0wVowhQiA7MrGGl64MsO68lJW7/HbWS+m6N70rWVtTOdIBBR83y7fvw7Y63FsbWt\nTdDEAOSduywPOnFdkLTaaDu5VPl19d8wl7Y00hbCVa06hRWbDwe4h4hbWjK58YB0\nO95ZY3Hgp5QkxvLF+Hs6\n=tJv9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-05T21:24:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/create-o3-app/commit/46395fc3659f80305f70e08812bab8efcc382d02","node_id":"C_kwDOQz_jx9oAKDQ2Mzk1ZmMzNjU5ZjgwMzA1ZjcwZTA4ODEyYmFiOGVmY2MzODJkMDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/create-o3-app/commit/f1403f25e38b1d6e7cc1c7edd8c88af9477554bf","sha":"f1403f25e38b1d6e7cc1c7edd8c88af9477554bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/commits/f1403f25e38b1d6e7cc1c7edd8c88af9477554bf"}],"sha":"46395fc3659f80305f70e08812bab8efcc382d02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/commits/46395fc3659f80305f70e08812bab8efcc382d02"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8509731?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/denniskigen","id":8509731,"login":"denniskigen","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MDk3MzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/commits/f1403f25e38b1d6e7cc1c7edd8c88af9477554bf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T13:28:36Z","email":"kigen.work@gmail.com","name":"Dennis Kigen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T13:28:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: wire the offline prompt and drop the dead optional-feature prompts (#11)\n\n* feat: wire the optional feature prompts into the generated output\n\nThe `dependabot`, `contributing`, `turbo`, and module-level `offline`\nanswers collected by the module prompts were stored on `ModuleConfig`\nbut never consumed, so scaffolded output ignored them. The template\nengine now excludes `turbo.json`, the new `.github/dependabot.yml`\ntemplate, and the new `CONTRIBUTING.md` template unless their flags\nare enabled, and the `offline` answer sets the per-route and\nper-extension `offline` values that `routes.json` renders (previously\nhardcoded to `true` even though the prompt defaults to `false`).\n\nThe `errorBoundary` prompt is removed instead of implemented: no\ntemplate existed for it and the O3 framework already provides error\nhandling. The field is dropped from `ModuleConfig`, the module config\nschema, and the non-interactive defaults.\n\nIncludes integration tests for the opt-in file gates and `routes.json`\noffline rendering, plus tests for the non-interactive prompt defaults.\n\n* Drop the turbo, dependabot, contributing, and accessibility prompts\n\nA survey of the local ecosystem (template-app, esm-core, patient-chart,\npatient-management, form-builder, dispensing, stock-management, billing)\nshowed these prompts offered things no O3 repo actually uses:\n\n- `turbo.json` used Turborepo 1.x `pipeline` syntax that turbo 2 rejects,\n  `turbo` was never a devDependency of the scaffold, and the convention\n  puts turbo at the monorepo root (as in all three flagship monorepos),\n  never in individual packages.\n- Only esm-core carries a `dependabot.yml`, and it is heavily curated\n  with ignore lists and dependency groups; the minimal npm-weekly config\n  here would open exactly the risky major-bump PRs those ignores exist\n  to suppress.\n- No repo ships a `CONTRIBUTING.md`; contribution guidance lives\n  centrally in o3-docs and the wiki.\n- The `accessibility` prompt is dead again after the jsx-a11y wiring was\n  reverted on the base branch: no repo lints with it, and the shared\n  `@openmrs/eslint-config` omits it deliberately.\n\nThe offline rendering coverage moves into the routes integration tests.","tree":{"sha":"e1fe4b54766cf93f16ef3433d2bf9e48c0d0967a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/git/trees/e1fe4b54766cf93f16ef3433d2bf9e48c0d0967a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/git/commits/f1403f25e38b1d6e7cc1c7edd8c88af9477554bf","verification":{"payload":"tree e1fe4b54766cf93f16ef3433d2bf9e48c0d0967a\nparent e0a6b694efa6b5543e30b42a545c701c7ff067c1\nauthor Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com> 1785936516 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785936516 +0300\n\nfix: wire the offline prompt and drop the dead optional-feature prompts (#11)\n\n* feat: wire the optional feature prompts into the generated output\n\nThe `dependabot`, `contributing`, `turbo`, and module-level `offline`\nanswers collected by the module prompts were stored on `ModuleConfig`\nbut never consumed, so scaffolded output ignored them. The template\nengine now excludes `turbo.json`, the new `.github/dependabot.yml`\ntemplate, and the new `CONTRIBUTING.md` template unless their flags\nare enabled, and the `offline` answer sets the per-route and\nper-extension `offline` values that `routes.json` renders (previously\nhardcoded to `true` even though the prompt defaults to `false`).\n\nThe `errorBoundary` prompt is removed instead of implemented: no\ntemplate existed for it and the O3 framework already provides error\nhandling. The field is dropped from `ModuleConfig`, the module config\nschema, and the non-interactive defaults.\n\nIncludes integration tests for the opt-in file gates and `routes.json`\noffline rendering, plus tests for the non-interactive prompt defaults.\n\n* Drop the turbo, dependabot, contributing, and accessibility prompts\n\nA survey of the local ecosystem (template-app, esm-core, patient-chart,\npatient-management, form-builder, dispensing, stock-management, billing)\nshowed these prompts offered things no O3 repo actually uses:\n\n- `turbo.json` used Turborepo 1.x `pipeline` syntax that turbo 2 rejects,\n  `turbo` was never a devDependency of the scaffold, and the convention\n  puts turbo at the monorepo root (as in all three flagship monorepos),\n  never in individual packages.\n- Only esm-core carries a `dependabot.yml`, and it is heavily curated\n  with ignore lists and dependency groups; the minimal npm-weekly config\n  here would open exactly the risky major-bump PRs those ignores exist\n  to suppress.\n- No repo ships a `CONTRIBUTING.md`; contribution guidance lives\n  centrally in o3-docs and the wiki.\n- The `accessibility` prompt is dead again after the jsx-a11y wiring was\n  reverted on the base branch: no repo lints with it, and the shared\n  `@openmrs/eslint-config` omits it deliberately.\n\nThe offline rendering coverage moves into the routes integration tests.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqczqECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7dMQAAeDE4Oh01y8Am73QAZYk3Mc\nVUsOag+TSINZeSPebvz5pBCvyX09z7xBHPi1LQTGF6E8YyMoLrXMuzX6CwanVeRR\n0eLM4u+gK7R271f+JTUtoDb1wWo/YhSe7qAZlgwz9TD21aPQAVfs8c5M3Rqpdo53\nIChhJiFnhi2Y24t2itK6PmuwtrC2QyT4Iho/9D4nRx8tXtbDIk3jh4o0Vxvbwl1v\nCBwJ6lDTP/bm0vHHYG1eQyceXotVYmt58PWqItd+TkKNKB76t5BUMvOX/tdJI8PA\nB/9oh3SQjqjbLqH782U29oqgu9mw8gS1Sxl+JnvmhxpzWfLUrm9RXIXCddeALj8g\nFeU0sx6+GH5x8dYuDZlBXlFl9uND9CVpITCcrWdtYgrdUd+VD23qw5Q3PYTHD4xb\n+qEHvRSITv+Lsq5pWG0xe/UeT5lLL0XhE6yUVJilTu7YXzHEm98cj3vqAmKuZvkY\nTArDBnrMVtG633QvAl3fjWsgqR8ylaJADFMUvdT8xI1MNLXZmiyOPhVRor5TG0Dn\ne2EzyQoGMH80v465xN/im+dONPV46r3SNN2b+6EhYI8eWi4GwWve+DI2G6Wo/ya8\nlCsflFuq4tkXb+97mmhYzZbuUmhdpm1B9F1Bw3iXzJ7zHg/nLNXuyWSRsTXW2iu7\nrqezl9vfLp1n7flAwd/+\n=MgA8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-05T13:28:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/create-o3-app/commit/f1403f25e38b1d6e7cc1c7edd8c88af9477554bf","node_id":"C_kwDOQz_jx9oAKGYxNDAzZjI1ZTM4YjFkNmU3Y2MxYzdlZGQ4Yzg4YWY5NDc3NTU0YmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/create-o3-app/commit/e0a6b694efa6b5543e30b42a545c701c7ff067c1","sha":"e0a6b694efa6b5543e30b42a545c701c7ff067c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/commits/e0a6b694efa6b5543e30b42a545c701c7ff067c1"}],"sha":"f1403f25e38b1d6e7cc1c7edd8c88af9477554bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/commits/f1403f25e38b1d6e7cc1c7edd8c88af9477554bf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8509731?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/denniskigen","id":8509731,"login":"denniskigen","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MDk3MzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/commits/e0a6b694efa6b5543e30b42a545c701c7ff067c1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T13:23:24Z","email":"kigen.work@gmail.com","name":"Dennis Kigen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T13:23:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: migrate to @openmrs/eslint-config and ESLint 9 (#12)\n\n* chore: migrate to @openmrs/eslint-config and ESLint 9\n\nScaffolded modules now get a flat eslint.config.mjs that composes the\nshared @openmrs/eslint-config preset instead of a standalone .eslintrc,\nwith react-hooks/exhaustive-deps kept at warn to preserve the previous\ntemplate behavior (the shared config deliberately omits it). The seven\nESLint plugin devDependencies are dropped in favor of the shared config,\neslint moves from the EOL 8.57 line to ^9.39.0, and the flat-config\nincompatible --ext flag is removed from the generated lint script.\n\nThe CLI''s own linting moves to ESLint 9 as well: eslint.config.mjs\ncomposes the shared base preset plus an overlay that keeps the stricter\ntype-aware rules this repo already enforced (no-floating-promises,\nno-misused-promises, no-unused-vars) and disables no-console, since a\nCLI''s output is the console. The two findings the new config surfaced\n(a duplicate import and a type-only import) are fixed, and the README''s\ndescription of the generated file tree is updated.\n\n* Wire the accessibility prompt into the generated output\n\nThe ''Add eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y for accessibility?'' prompt stored its\nanswer in config.accessibility but nothing consumed it. When enabled,\nthe generated app now gets eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y in devDependencies\nand jsxA11y.flatConfigs.recommended layered into eslint.config.mjs,\nboth gated via Handlebars on the accessibility flag. The shared\n@openmrs/eslint-config intentionally leaves jsx-a11y out, so this\nprompt is what adds it. Includes tests for both states.\n\n* Remove the jsx-a11y layer from the generated output\n\nA survey of the local ecosystem (template-app, esm-core, patient-chart,\npatient-management, form-builder, dispensing, stock-management, billing)\nfound no repo linting with eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y, and the shared\n@openmrs/eslint-config deliberately leaves it out. Scaffolded modules\nshould not diverge from every existing repo, so this reverts the\naccessibility wiring. The now-dead prompt is removed alongside the other\ndead prompts in the stacked PR.\n\nThis reverts commit edc6592642c0298a8ecc2c1c1da068fe06b78add.\n\n* Bump @openmrs/eslint-config to ^2.0.0\n\nv2.0.0 restores `@typescript-eslint/no-require-imports` to `error` for\nsource files, which 1.0.0 had disabled everywhere by mistake, and\nraises its plugin dependency floors. Both the CLI and the scaffolded\ntemplate move to `^2.0.0`.\n\nNo code changes needed on either surface: the CLI repo lints clean\nunder the bumped preset, and a fresh scaffold with a route, extension,\nmodal, workspace, and feature flag passes `yarn lint` under an\ninstalled 2.0.0 (the `require.context` call in the generated\n`index.ts` is not flagged by the restored rule).","tree":{"sha":"2a2835b7311f9a80a14b9fa2dee120323e0339ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/git/trees/2a2835b7311f9a80a14b9fa2dee120323e0339ce"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/git/commits/e0a6b694efa6b5543e30b42a545c701c7ff067c1","verification":{"payload":"tree 2a2835b7311f9a80a14b9fa2dee120323e0339ce\nparent be3cc5a3f27c4fcdb7c448e51cb38c86bbd9db26\nauthor Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com> 1785936204 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785936204 +0300\n\nchore: migrate to @openmrs/eslint-config and ESLint 9 (#12)\n\n* chore: migrate to @openmrs/eslint-config and ESLint 9\n\nScaffolded modules now get a flat eslint.config.mjs that composes the\nshared @openmrs/eslint-config preset instead of a standalone .eslintrc,\nwith react-hooks/exhaustive-deps kept at warn to preserve the previous\ntemplate behavior (the shared config deliberately omits it). The seven\nESLint plugin devDependencies are dropped in favor of the shared config,\neslint moves from the EOL 8.57 line to ^9.39.0, and the flat-config\nincompatible --ext flag is removed from the generated lint script.\n\nThe CLI''s own linting moves to ESLint 9 as well: eslint.config.mjs\ncomposes the shared base preset plus an overlay that keeps the stricter\ntype-aware rules this repo already enforced (no-floating-promises,\nno-misused-promises, no-unused-vars) and disables no-console, since a\nCLI''s output is the console. The two findings the new config surfaced\n(a duplicate import and a type-only import) are fixed, and the README''s\ndescription of the generated file tree is updated.\n\n* Wire the accessibility prompt into the generated output\n\nThe ''Add eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y for accessibility?'' prompt stored its\nanswer in config.accessibility but nothing consumed it. When enabled,\nthe generated app now gets eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y in devDependencies\nand jsxA11y.flatConfigs.recommended layered into eslint.config.mjs,\nboth gated via Handlebars on the accessibility flag. The shared\n@openmrs/eslint-config intentionally leaves jsx-a11y out, so this\nprompt is what adds it. Includes tests for both states.\n\n* Remove the jsx-a11y layer from the generated output\n\nA survey of the local ecosystem (template-app, esm-core, patient-chart,\npatient-management, form-builder, dispensing, stock-management, billing)\nfound no repo linting with eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y, and the shared\n@openmrs/eslint-config deliberately leaves it out. Scaffolded modules\nshould not diverge from every existing repo, so this reverts the\naccessibility wiring. The now-dead prompt is removed alongside the other\ndead prompts in the stacked PR.\n\nThis reverts commit edc6592642c0298a8ecc2c1c1da068fe06b78add.\n\n* Bump @openmrs/eslint-config to ^2.0.0\n\nv2.0.0 restores `@typescript-eslint/no-require-imports` to `error` for\nsource files, which 1.0.0 had disabled everywhere by mistake, and\nraises its plugin dependency floors. Both the CLI and the scaffolded\ntemplate move to `^2.0.0`.\n\nNo code changes needed on either surface: the CLI repo lints clean\nunder the bumped preset, and a fresh scaffold with a route, extension,\nmodal, workspace, and feature flag passes `yarn lint` under an\ninstalled 2.0.0 (the `require.context` call in the generated\n`index.ts` is not flagged by the restored rule).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqczlMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAN+gQADb2PqZncb70kwwzE6Zi7/lI\nF0WSWTfC/iAEWyOkowU6DyIK05QLZCZ6M5Y5DdsKb/QQ9xh9Z3z2ZC8UfSFd4xv1\n7Mcbn7YeWsk+mKVJWe+0WU+YTQf4jGehO4iz/WltntxCwM77AKxKbkVPnCirxl60\n4vWe9oOLpu0ZGx4meH2lpTn38pVcSc+J9FvDBb/5kvKYEndhGAwOc0TLUoehLnFD\n6Ow9V6XSfLRiUIFeZ+HPq1TGJgvMidVt+ufCk82VeV0LhFo7al4jhRbWWTFZgbig\nXhb3Zvrpv+C0Hu4Egm01hhEaHcVAhJ3Al4uOgu21kiV2m2ajYfFdbiYMc7Iqk+fY\nRSjzgvQXe0+NgYTCfJi99okh/RVDyAFxAxFeIXZqBo8ExKbE6w5S9HWIOSuBx9Bw\nBYC1lufpQDZGoc592yIT5MEqAvZziklkh3e/ViQUMrpMRKg6lznzAl2VHZQz8y+C\nauRNFApijd6wWijYxxJCV1yfGyPFvkl4DF2nLZH1wgpMm3lLJ9exOE3HfQpsy5uP\n6mRVMjsRn8JlbXbcpyvVF3r7wjopYXGpwYIkMm8ECAnZqKXTCKP0W9DDj0Ejqqxw\nTIPWcx3pjHGRFvYWLFZTyJn0tfqNpGRFMlHt/El5J0kYyY26D0SqKg5Z2cw4pmR5\nQ60ggbSixXMEb+USPJGB\n=zpaR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-05T13:23:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/