m/u/8509731?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/denniskigen","id":8509731,"login":"denniskigen","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MDk3MzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/commits/87c253c33f65c7fcfecb947278b9e2b24fdc8766/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-27T22:33:12Z","email":"kigen.work@gmail.com","name":"Dennis Kigen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-27T22:33:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: publish to npm under the @openmrs scope (#5)\n\n* chore: publish to npm under the @openmrs scope\n\nThe CLI was never published: no release tag has ever been pushed, and the\npackage was configured in a way that would have blocked the first publish.\n\n- Rename the package from the unscoped `create-o3-app` (owned by a third\n  party on npm) to `@openmrs/create-o3-app`, matching the README and every\n  other OpenMRS package. This also keeps the `npm create @openmrs/o3-app`\n  entry point working.\n- Add `publishConfig.access: public` so `npm publish` succeeds for the newly\n  scoped package, which defaults to restricted.\n- Build during `prepare` so the `dist/` artifacts exist when installing from\n  git and before packing.\n- Fix the release-notes install snippet to use the scoped name.\n\n* ci: use the org-shared NPM_AUTH_TOKEN secret for publishing\n\nThe release workflow referenced secrets.NPM_TOKEN, which doesn''t exist.\nOpenMRS repos publish with the org-level NPM_AUTH_TOKEN secret (see\nopenmrs-esm-core ci.yml), so npm publish would otherwise run with an\nempty auth token and fail.\n\n* fix: ship a .gitignore in scaffolded modules\n\nTwo issues meant generated modules never received a .gitignore:\n\n- The file-exclusion filter used `relativePath.includes(''.git'')`, which also\n  matched `.gitignore`, so the template was dropped at scaffold time. Remove\n  the `.git` pattern; globby already ignores the `.git/**` directory.\n- npm strips a literal `.gitignore` from published tarballs, so even with the\n  filter fixed an install-from-npm scaffold would omit it. Ship the template\n  as `.gitignore.hbs`; the engine strips `.hbs` and writes `.gitignore`, and\n  the renamed file survives `npm pack`.\n\nAdd an engine test asserting `.gitignore.hbs` renders to `.gitignore`.","tree":{"sha":"74f302426c1a239db3422393f767d9eef25e7d1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/git/trees/74f302426c1a239db3422393f767d9eef25e7d1f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/create-o3-app/git/commits/87c253c33f65c7fcfecb947278b9e2b24fdc8766","verification":{"payload":"tree 74f302426c1a239db3422393f767d9eef25e7d1f\nparent 469e1467e9ace1a73a7bdb07c5f505259ba7114f\nauthor Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com> 1779921192 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779921192 +0300\n\nchore: publish to npm under the @openmrs scope (#5)\n\n* chore: publish to npm under the @openmrs scope\n\nThe CLI was never published: no release tag has ever been pushed, and the\npackage was configured in a way that would have blocked the first publish.\n\n- Rename the package from the unscoped `create-o3-app` (owned by a third\n  party on npm) to `@openmrs/create-o3-app`, matching the README and every\n  other OpenMRS package. This also keeps the `npm create @openmrs/o3-app`\n  entry point working.\n- Add `publishConfig.access: public` so `npm publish` succeeds for the newly\n  scoped package, which defaults to restricted.\n- Build during `prepare` so the `dist/` artifacts exist when installing from\n  git and before packing.\n- Fix the release-notes install snippet to use the scoped name.\n\n* ci: use the org-shared NPM_AUTH_TOKEN secret for publishing\n\nThe release workflow referenced secrets.NPM_TOKEN, which doesn''t exist.\nOpenMRS repos publish with the org-level NPM_AUTH_TOKEN secret (see\nopenmrs-esm-core ci.yml), so npm publish would otherwise run with an\nempty auth token and fail.\n\n* fix: ship a .gitignore in scaffolded modules\n\nTwo issues meant generated modules never received a .gitignore:\n\n- The file-exclusion filter used `relativePath.includes(''.git'')`, which also\n  matched `.gitignore`, so the template was dropped at scaffold time. Remove\n  the `.git` pattern; globby already ignores the `.git/**` directory.\n- npm strips a literal `.gitignore` from published tarballs, so even with the\n  filter fixed an install-from-npm scaffold would omit it. Ship the template\n  as `.gitignore.hbs`; the engine strips `.hbs` and writes `.gitignore`, and\n  the renamed file survives `npm pack`.\n\nAdd an engine test asserting `.gitignore.hbs` renders to `.gitignore`.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqF3EoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAW5kQAJVEKFxrS378f8XFoMs8Cd86\nswXlF87rmW0x2L1gaXrsZk9itxmmG+s2ZuvH6R7TuwGDoBzv0efa6srBmvOLBcVe\n5Duhjv2id4UycAUZy4+UJGNws9t1Z+kzNovEZFqTlSV4AnCMsqeTLOEOUgXawYcM\nNciItkVq9AeQrkhray0pPFtbk/V64SR7ob2daOW0BNG5b8Tq23TMh3rWUsFUV8Hw\nnkzbTUR9KR0ocQ3b7BefNzKEVhzS3jSJlAH8oKUa0TUFg2h/q8gN9Il1Ix/QKqQ2\nPj1Cbu0ZyvIWAsgwZDzOSW+GxeE9Mbs0QL+FVEDU+LI6fIX3b7MYdW0u2QRp0jLz\nmnZerQAFbNmzxK5zFNNEIa2uBem2pwv+DJCRGYbd0JjhWuRIBUyGkwhqY24ijLBJ\nNK+1HRMl8v1oPw6pSGjoC1UZdgI5fNfdGZzyuF5Q6wJeKWrGVDRivB76F08TxisI