"node_id":"U_kgDOC972lw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shellui/shellui/commits/ca0c81e1e6a09cfd18a2bdd3f8a94b8673a77665/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T07:19:15Z","email":"cursoragent@cursor.com","name":"Cursor Agent"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T07:19:15Z","email":"cursoragent@cursor.com","name":"Cursor Agent"},"message":"fix(ai): stop Settings AI details 1fr track from stretching panel height\n\nThe [data-shellui-ai-details] open state uses grid-template-rows: 1fr for the\ncollapse animation. Inside the Settings flex scroll column that track was\nexpanding to fill leftover viewport height, leaving a huge empty white slab\nunder Built-in browser model after toggling Prompt API.\n\nHug content instead: align-self: start, flex: 0 0 auto, height: max-content,\nwidth: 100% on the details grid, plus shrink-0/self-start on the Ai root.\nKeeps the 0fr→1fr animation without eating free space.","tree":{"sha":"27bf4a7b06d7b4daf5c083dfecebd9cab1d46cf7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shellui/shellui/git/trees/27bf4a7b06d7b4daf5c083dfecebd9cab1d46cf7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shellui/shellui/git/commits/ca0c81e1e6a09cfd18a2bdd3f8a94b8673a77665","verification":{"payload":"tree 27bf4a7b06d7b4daf5c083dfecebd9cab1d46cf7\nparent 2fe54c5f69c3e7eec16aecd275d55ce7458720a7\nauthor Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com> 1789802355 +0000\ncommitter Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com> 1789802355 +0000\n\nfix(ai): stop Settings AI details 1fr track from stretching panel height\n\nThe [data-shellui-ai-details] open state uses grid-template-rows: 1fr for the\ncollapse animation. Inside the Settings flex scroll column that track was\nexpanding to fill leftover viewport height, leaving a huge empty white slab\nunder Built-in browser model after toggling Prompt API.\n\nHug content instead: align-self: start, flex: 0 0 auto, height: max-content,\nwidth: 100% on the details grid, plus shrink-0/self-start on the Ai root.\nKeeps the 0fr→1fr animation without eating free space.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg+qImwGMCy/grKZ50VxRHz3VfWW\nAL3QNbzIy2Nwcn+nQAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQFhh+6ihdB5FJZhB7B1VnwA+/VLLyVwsYxuua3ctCBH37pIIjj3CIy2+zNDW8OVoir\ng+mfweqnMj/Jce262cIAQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-19T07:19:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199161495?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cursoragent","id":199161495,"login":"cursoragent","node_id":"U_kgDOC972lw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/shellui/shellui/commit/ca0c81e1e6a09cfd18a2bdd3f8a94b8673a77665","node_id":"C_kwDOQ0QnXtoAKGNhMGM4MWUxZTZhMDljZmQxOGEyYmRkM2Y4YTk0Yjg2NzNhNzc2NjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/shellui/shellui/commit/2fe54c5f69c3e7eec16aecd275d55ce7458720a7","sha":"2fe54c5f69c3e7eec16aecd275d55ce7458720a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shellui/shellui/commits/2fe54c5f69c3e7eec16aecd275d55ce7458720a7"}],"sha":"ca0c81e1e6a09cfd18a2bdd3f8a94b8673a77665","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shellui/shellui/commits/ca0c81e1e6a09cfd18a2bdd3f8a94b8673a77665"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199161495?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cursoragent","id":199161495,"login":"cursoragent","node_id":"U_kgDOC972lw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shellui/shellui/commits/2fe54c5f69c3e7eec16aecd275d55ce7458720a7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T07:17:15Z","email":"cursoragent@cursor.com","name":"Cursor Agent"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T07:17:15Z","email":"cursoragent@cursor.com","name":"Cursor Agent"},"message":"fix(ai): Prompt API Enable UX instead of Install/0% progress\n\nChrome often reports no transferable downloadprogress (model already on\ndevice, or events stuck at loaded=0), so labeling the warm path as Install\nand showing a 0% bar was wrong UX.\n\nSettings → AI for the Prompt API provider now uses the Enable/Disable\nswitch as the main control. When availability is downloadable, an Enable\nbutton (or turning the switch on) runs create({ monitor }). Progress is\nindeterminate (“Setting up built-in model…”) unless Chrome fires real\nloaded > 0 — never a stuck 0% bar. Already-ready models need no Enable\nbutton. WebLLM catalog Install/Download unchanged.","tree":{"sha":"95121366857d0aaae6393d7d67664230a897c570","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shellui/shellui/git/trees/95121366857d0aaae6393d7d67664230a897c570"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shellui/shellui/git/commits/2fe54c5f69c3e7eec16aecd275d55ce7458720a7","verification":{"payload":"tree 95121366857d0aaae6393d7d67664230a897c570\nparent e3f0b7404fec7664593652288690ffdcc807af18\nauthor Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com> 1789802235 +0000\ncommitter Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com> 1789802235 +0000\n\nfix(ai): Prompt API Enable UX instead of Install/0% progress\n\nChrome often reports no transferable downloadprogress (model already on\ndevice, or events stuck at loaded=0), so labeling the warm path as Install\nand showing a 0% bar was wrong UX.\n\nSettings → AI for the Prompt API provider now uses the Enable/Disable\nswitch as the main control. When availability is downloadable, an Enable\nbutton (or turning the switch on) runs create({ monitor }). Progress is\nindeterminate (“Setting up built-in model…”) unless Chrome fires real\nloaded > 0 — never a stuck 0% bar. Already-ready models need no Enable\nbutton. WebLLM catalog Install/Download unchanged.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg+qImwGMCy/grKZ50VxRHz3VfWW\nAL3QNbzIy2Nwcn+nQAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLsWdT/nEw3vEo58DekIDl6f15mhbrKGYDbSFDs6j/BWlqFRUfVJpKj2koGCSOXMy/\nK+lOrt4vX336oZrqecCAI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-19T07:17:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199161495?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cursoragent","id":199161495,"login":"cursoragent","node_id":"U_kgDOC972lw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/shellui/shellui/commit/2fe54c5f69c3e7eec16aecd275d55ce7458720a7","node_id":"C_kwDOQ0QnXtoAKDJmZTU0YzVmNjljM2U3ZWVjMTZhZWNkMjc1ZDU1Y2U3NDU4NzIwYTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/shellui/shellui/commit/e3f0b7404fec7664593652288690ffdcc807af18","sha":"e3f0b7404fec7664593652288690ffdcc807af18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shellui/shellui/commits/e3f0b7404fec7664593652288690ffdcc807af18"}],"sha":"2fe54c5f69c3e7eec16aecd275d55ce7458720a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shellui/shellui/commits/2fe54c5f69c3e7eec16aecd275d55ce7458720a7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199161495?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cursoragent","id":199161495,"login":"cursoragent","node_id":"U_kgDOC972lw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shellui/shellui/commits/e3f0b7404fec7664593652288690ffdcc807af18/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T20:41:33Z","email":"cursoragent@cursor.com","name":"Cursor Agent"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T20:41:33Z","email":"cursoragent@cursor.com","name":"Cursor Agent"},"message":"feat(ai): add Chrome built-in Prompt API as a browser model provider\n\nNew PromptApiAdapter (provider id `prompt-api`) surfaces the browser''s on-device\nLanguageModel (Gemini Nano) through the same shellui.ai path as Ollama/WebLLM.\n\nShow only when present: feature-detect the Chrome global (LanguageModel, or the\nlegacy ai.languageModel) and its availability(). When missing or `unavailable`\n(Firefox, Safari, iPhone, Chrome without the model, older Chrome), the provider\nis omitted entirely from Settings → AI — no warning, no disabled stub.\n\n- listModels: one model when available/downloadable/downloading; [] otherwise.\n- download: triggers the browser''s own model download with progress (monitor).\n- prompt/promptStreaming: fresh stateless LanguageModel session per turn, seeded\n  with history as initialPrompts; streaming normalized to deltas. No wedge-prone\n  lock (unlike WebLLM), so resetConversation is a no-op.\n- Registered by default in createDefaultAiRegistry (self-hides via listModels);\n  filtered by new optional ai.promptApiEnabled setting (default true).\n- Settings → AI: provider section + toggle rendered only when detected; en/fr i18n.\n- Docs: Ollama recommended; Prompt API when Chrome provides it (absent on\n  Safari/iPhone); WebLLM in-browser catalog.\n- Tests mock the LanguageModel global for available/missing/downloadable cases.\n\nDoes not replace WebLLM.","tree":{"sha":"deb3ec5fba0be1428a32c1bb7cc58bdd6d0f6692","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shellui/shellui/git/trees/deb3ec5fba0be1428a32c1bb7cc58bdd6d0f6692"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shellui/shellui/git/commits/e3f0b7404fec7664593652288690ffdcc807af18","verification":{"payload":"tree deb3ec5fba0be1428a32c1bb7cc58bdd6d0f6692\nparent 41cde72333d1ff84728ea53773613c4760609f76\nauthor Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com> 1789764093 +0000\ncommitter Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com> 1789764093 +0000\n\nfeat(ai): add Chrome built-in Prompt API as a browser model provider\n\nNew PromptApiAdapter (provider id `prompt-api`) surfaces the browser''s on-device\nLanguageModel (Gemini Nano) through the same shellui.ai path as Ollama/WebLLM.\n\nShow only when present: feature-detect the Chrome global (LanguageModel, or the\nlegacy ai.languageModel) and its availability(). When missing or `unavailable`\n(Firefox, Safari, iPhone, Chrome without the model, older Chrome), the provider\nis omitted entirely from Settings → AI — no warning, no disabled stub.\n\n- listModels: one model when available/downloadable/downloading; [] otherwise.\n- download: triggers the browser''s own model download with progress (monitor).\n- prompt/promptStreaming: fresh stateless LanguageModel session per turn, seeded\n  with history as initialPrompts; streaming normalized to deltas. No wedge-prone\n  lock (unlike WebLLM), so resetConversation is a no-op.\n- Registered by default in createDefaultAiRegistry (self-hides via listModels);\n  filtered by new optional ai.promptApiEnabled setting (default true).\n- Settings → AI: provider section + toggle rendered only when detected; en/fr i18n.\n- Docs: Ollama recommended; Prompt API when Chrome provides it (absent on\n  Safari/iPhone); WebLLM in-browser catalog.\n- Tests mock the LanguageModel global for available/missing/downloadable cases.\n\nDoes not replace WebLLM.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg+qImwGMCy/grKZ50VxRHz3VfWW\nAL3QNbzIy2Nwcn+nQAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQO2udCQS9aLMIroPa1Cyn0ODmC8tyIRqU+sRAwUy0bSfM2kR7uszYgeZaGPSp4fieG\n0Fpe8VEXus+tyyO2krKgU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T20:41:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199161495?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cursoragent","id":199161495,"login":"cursoragent","node_id":"U_kgDOC972lw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/shellui/shellui/commit/e3f0b7404fec7664593652288690ffdcc807af18","node_id":"C_kwDOQ0QnXtoAKGUzZjBiNzQwNGZlYzc2NjQ1OTM2NTIyODg2OTBmZmRjYzgwN2FmMTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/shellui/shellui/commit/41cde72333d1ff84728ea53773613c4760609f76","sha":"41cde72333d1ff84728ea53773613c4760609f76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shellui/shellui/commits/41cde72333d1ff84728ea53773613c4760609f76"}],"sha":"e3f0b7404fec7664593652288690ffdcc807af18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shellui/shellui/commits/e3f0b7404fec7664593652288690ffdcc807af18"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199161495?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cursoragent","id":199161495,"login":"cursoragent","node_id":"U_kgDOC972lw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shellui/shellui/commits/41cde72333d1ff84728ea53773613c4760609f76/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T20:30:06Z","email":"cursoragent@cursor.com","name":"Cursor Agent"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T20:30:06Z","email":"cursoragent@cursor.com","name":"Cursor Agent"},"message":"fix(ai): recreate WebLLM worker on conversation switch / Stop instead of reload\n\nSoft resetChat and interrupt+reload on the living worker never reliably fixed\n\"new chat stuck on Thinking...\" because the root cause is upstream: the WebLLM\nmodel lock is not always released after a streamed completion (mlc-ai/web-llm#701,\nstill unmerged in 0.2.85) and interruptGenerate can leave the lock stuck\n(mlc-ai/mlc-llm#3113). Fighting a wedged worker with reload cannot win.\n\nNuclear reliable v1 strategy: on a genuine conversation switch (create for a new\nsessionId, prompt for a different sessionId, destroy of the active session) and on\nStop/abort, fully dispose the worker (worker.terminate(), no awaited unload so a\nwedged worker can''t hang us) and recreate a fresh CreateWebWorkerMLCEngine for the\nsame model on the next prompt. Weights come from the WebLLM browser cache (short\nwarm, not a full HF re-download). Same-session multi-turn keeps the warm worker;\nOllama is unaffected (stateless HTTP).\n\nTests updated to assert engine recreate (create-engine call count) on switch,\ndeferred recreate after resetConversation, and worker dispose after Stop/abort.\nDocs + CHANGELOG cite the upstream bugs and explain why prior approaches failed.","tree":{"sha":"fa372c9b4d18f00dd893a8d1953fddbab4755ef7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shellui/shellui/git/trees/fa372c9b4d18f00dd893a8d1953fddbab4755ef7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shellui/shellui/git/commits/41cde72333d1ff84728ea53773613c4760609f76","verification":{"payload":"tree fa372c9b4d18f00dd893a8d1953fddbab4755ef7\nparent d823faed08b81c74412262a37a33b4649e6eee24\nauthor Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com> 1789763406 +0000\ncommitter Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com> 1789763406 +0000\n\nfix(ai): recreate WebLLM worker on conversation switch / Stop instead of reload\n\nSoft resetChat and interrupt+reload on the living worker never reliably fixed\n\"new chat stuck on Thinking...\" because the root cause is upstream: the WebLLM\nmodel lock is not always released after a streamed completion (mlc-ai/web-llm#701,\nstill unmerged in 0.2.85) and interruptGenerate can leave the lock stuck\n(mlc-ai/mlc-llm#3113). Fighting a wedged worker with reload cannot win.\n\nNuclear reliable v1 strategy: on a genuine conversation switch (create for a new\nsessionId, prompt for a different sessionId, destroy of the active session) and on\nStop/abort, fully dispose the worker (worker.terminate(), no awaited unload so a\nwedged worker can''t hang us) and recreate a fresh CreateWebWorkerMLCEngine for the\nsame model on the next prompt. Weights come from the WebLLM browser cache (short\nwarm, not a full HF re-download). Same-session multi-turn keeps the warm worker;\nOllama is unaffected (stateless HTTP).\n\nTests updated to assert engine recreate (create-engine call count) on switch,\ndeferred recreate after resetConversation, and worker dispose after Stop/abort.\nDocs + CHANGELOG cite the upstream bugs and explain why prior approaches failed.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg+qImwGMCy/grKZ50VxRHz3VfWW\nAL3QNbzIy2Nwcn+nQAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQK3rMVvoGS79jofgcbUjdRAIKcqlB00Mp3rnvgVxTi4aZO+COrJG7Pqtnh2KHqGcqd\nppyPKrhFDa9OTrCq+dOQ8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T20:30:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199161495?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cursoragent","id":199161495,"login":"cursoragent","node_id":"U_kgDOC972lw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/shellui/shellui/commit/41cde72333d1ff84728ea53773613c4760609f76","node_id":"C_kwDOQ0QnXtoAKDQxY2RlNzIzMzNkMWZmODQ3MjhlYTUzNzczNjEzYzQ3NjA2MDlmNzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/shellui/shellui/commit/d823faed08b81c74412262a37a33b4649e6eee24","sha":"d823faed08b81c74412262a37a33b4649e6eee24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shellui/shellui/commits/d823faed08b81c74412262a37a33b4649e6eee24"}],"sha":"41cde72333d1ff84728ea53773613c4760609f76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shellui/shellui/commits/41cde72333d1ff84728ea53773613c4760609f76"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199161495?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cursoragent","id":199161495,"login":"cursoragent","node_id":"U_kgDOC972lw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shellui/shellui/commits/d823faed08b81c74412262a37a33b4649e6eee24/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T20:21:46Z","email":"cursoragent@cursor.com","name":"Cursor Agent"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T20:21:46Z","email":"cursoragent@cursor.com","name":"Cursor Agent"},"message":"fix(ai): treat Safari as recommended for WebLLM Install\n\nSébastien confirmed WebLLM works on Safari — drop the Safari experimental\nwarning. Chrome/Edge/Safari are recommended; Firefox stays experimental only.","tree":{"sha":"ab0708d35370bf6f2176965a349d4d6062386e63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shellui/shellui/git/trees/ab0708d35370bf6f2176965a349d4d6062386e63"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shellui/shellui/git/commits/d823faed08b81c74412262a37a33b4649e6eee24","verification":{"payload":"tree ab0708d35370bf6f2176965a349d4d6062386e63\nparent 8c8ea4dcc01c58a1c89ac95a43b3dc64c0deb45c\nauthor Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com> 1789762906 +0000\ncommitter Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com> 1789762906 +0000\n\nfix(ai): treat Safari as recommended for WebLLM Install\n\nSébastien confirmed WebLLM works on Safari — drop the Safari experimental\nwarning. Chrome/Edge/Safari are recommended; Firefox stays experimental only.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg+qImwGMCy/grKZ50VxRHz3VfWW\nAL3QNbzIy2Nwcn+nQAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQHnVc/CQTQiHGoQZrCXIIZAw5teZRF0kt5rjW7fDtvSLiswBrA07H7Zx/8Svah9s48\n/YbzjreqTDkxDA/iT4Mwk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T20:21:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199161495?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cursoragent","id":199161495,"login":"cursoragent","node_id":"U_kgDOC972lw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/shellui/shellui/commit/d823faed08b81c74412262a37a33b4649e6eee24","node_id":"C_kwDOQ0QnXtoAKGQ4MjNmYWVkMDhiODFjNzQ0MTIyNjJhMzdhMzNiNDY0OWU2ZWVlMjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/shellui/shellui/commit/8c8ea4dcc01c58a1c89ac95a43b3dc64c0deb45c","sha":"8c8ea4dcc01c58a1c89ac95a43b3dc64c0deb45c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shellui/shellui/commits/8c8ea4dcc01c58a1c89ac95a43b3dc64c0deb45c"}],"sha":"d823faed08b81c74412262a37a33b4649e6eee24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shellui/shellui/commits/d823faed08b81c74412262a37a33b4649e6eee24"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199161495?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cursoragent","id":199161495,"login":"cursoragent","node_id":"U_kgDOC972lw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shellui/shellui/commits/8c8ea4dcc01c58a1c89ac95a43b3dc64c0deb45c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T20:08:25Z","email":"cursoragent@cursor.com","name":"Cursor Agent"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T20:08:25Z","email":"cursoragent@cursor.com","name":"Cursor Agent"},"message":"fix(ai): experimental (not blocked) non-Chromium Install + reliable WebLLM chat switch\n\n1) Soften browser gate: probeWebLlmBrowserSupport returns { recommended,\n   canInstall: true }. Firefox/Safari are warned, not blocked — Install is\n   attempted and real errors surface. Settings shows a warning banner; catalog\n   models are never ''unsupported''. Docs note WebKit vs Blink.\n\n2) Fix conversation switch on WebLLM (Ollama is stateless so unaffected):\n   the worker keeps chat/KV + a generation lock, so soft resetChat wasn''t\n   enough. Track the owning session on WebLLMEngineService; on switch, eagerly\n   interruptGenerate (break stuck lock) then reload the same model id (clears\n   KV, weights cached). Thread sessionId prompt/promptStreaming/create/destroy.\n\nTests: session-switch reload regression + experimental-browser install.","tree":{"sha":"19f2565e61bcad6864792490cbdf95ac6d4ac520","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shellui/shellui/git/trees/19f2565e61bcad6864792490cbdf95ac6d4ac520"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shellui/shellui/git/commits/8c8ea4dcc01c58a1c89ac95a43b3dc64c0deb45c","verification":{"payload":"tree 19f2565e61bcad6864792490cbdf95ac6d4ac520\nparent 000b15a4b5285677529c33805c3eb5b86bc776bf\nauthor Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com> 1789762105 +0000\ncommitter Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com> 1789762105 +0000\n\nfix(ai): experimental (not blocked) non-Chromium Install + reliable WebLLM chat switch\n\n1) Soften browser gate: probeWebLlmBrowserSupport returns { recommended,\n   canInstall: true }. Firefox/Safari are warned, not blocked — Install is\n   attempted and real errors surface. Settings shows a warning banner; catalog\n   models are never ''unsupported''. Docs note WebKit vs Blink.\n\n2) Fix conversation switch on WebLLM (Ollama is stateless so unaffected):\n   the worker keeps chat/KV + a generation lock, so soft resetChat wasn''t\n   enough. Track the owning session on WebLLMEngineService; on switch, eagerly\n   interruptGenerate (break stuck lock) then reload the same model id (clears\n   KV, weights cached). Thread sessionId prompt/promptStreaming/create/destroy.\n\nTests: session-switch reload regression + experimental-browser install.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg+qImwGMCy/grKZ50VxRHz3VfWW\nAL3QNbzIy2Nwcn+nQAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQO6n7b+nMDqhKf4Nl5+mvRMduJgBqxqD4hlyoG0vKbm3zwfHf2aS8vxNVGCwhrVOXr\n7rXvgSnnHTQUBlzUowdw0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T20:08:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199161495?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cursoragent","id":199161495,"login":"cursoragent","node_id":"U_kgDOC972lw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/shellui/shellui/commit/8c8ea4dcc01c58a1c89ac95a43b3dc64c0deb45c","node_id":"C_kwDOQ0QnXtoAKDhjOGVhNGRjYzAxYzU4YTFjODlhYzk1YTQzYjNkYzY0YzBkZWI0NWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/shellui/shellui/commit/000b15a4b5285677529c33805c3eb5b86bc776bf","sha":"000b15a4b5285